# Line endings.
#
# The repo is developed on Windows and runs on Linux. Without this, a clone
# with core.autocrlf=true checks these out with CRLF, and a shell script whose
# shebang ends "#!/bin/bash\r" fails on Linux with a bad-interpreter error that
# names an invisible character. The same applies to anything Docker or a CI
# runner executes.
#
# Normalise text in general, then pin the files that must be LF on disk.
* text=auto

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf

# Binary: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.ico       binary
*.onnx      binary
*.task      binary
*.mp4       binary
*.webm      binary
